    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0486" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg418"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 175.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 30, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Messrs. Baring, in reply to a letter
                    from the department on the subject, have stated that it would not be convenient
                    for them to purchase bills <pb facs="0487" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/> on you for
                    the surplus of the Chinese indemnity. They suggest that you be authorized to
                    purchase bills on London with that surplus, and remit the same to them.</p>
                <p>The department has informed them that this suggestion, if adopted at all,
                    probably would not be carried into effect until after the next session of
                    Congress.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
